Package: vabaxos-restore
Architecture: all
Maintainer: VabaxOS <https://github.com/Vabax-dev/VabaxOS>
Section: admin
Priority: optional
Depends: timeshift, python3, python3-gi, gir1.2-gtk-4.0, gir1.2-adw-1 (>= 1.5), pkexec, util-linux
Recommends: cryptsetup, lvm2
Description: System restore: back to before an update that broke something
 VabaxOS copies the system with Timeshift (rsync, also on ext4) before
 every installation of packages and once a week, and keeps the newest
 ones (ADR-0027). The window System restore lists the copies with their
 reason and restores one; the command "ripristino" does it from the text
 console, also from the recovery mode of the VabaxOS USB stick when the
 installed desktop does not start, also with an encrypted disk. Documents
 and personal folders are never in the copies and never change.
